! <solver:p610_t3>
! SLOPE64 "Example 1: A homogeneous slope" mapped to GeotechSlopeApp p610_t3 elastoplastic input.
! Source parameters (Colorado School of Mines SLOPE64 tutorial):
!   https://inside.mines.edu/~vgriffit/slope64/ex1.dat
!   w1=12  s1=20  w2=12  h1=10  h2=10  (m)
!   nx1=32 nx2=12 ny1=10 ny2=10  (SLOPE64 mesh counts — not used here; this file uses a coarse FEM fan mesh)
!   phi=30 deg  c=5 kPa  psi=0  gamma=20 kN/m3  E=1e5 kPa  nu=0.3
!   k_h=0  gam_w=0  limit=1000  fos_tol=0.02  (LE iteration / tolerance — mapped loosely to VP tol/limit below)
!
! 2D cross-section (x right, y up), CCW domain boundary:
!   Left toe (-s1,h2), left crest (0,h1+h2), right crest (w1,h1+h2), right toe (w1+s1,h2),
!   foundation right (w1+s1+w2,h2), bottom right, bottom left.
! Interior fan node at (10,5) splits the heptagon into 7 T3 elements (teaching mesh; refine in GUI/RS2D for production).
!
! Solver path: layers=0 applies far-field-style tractions on listed boundary edges from zero initial stress
! (see p610_t3_elastoplastic.cpp). Traction sigma components are tension-positive kPa; approximate at-rest
! compression on sloping/vertical boundaries for demonstration (not identical to SLOPE64 LE FoS workflow).
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastoplastic
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
! Mesh size block:
! nels nn np_types
7  8  1
! Material/property block:
! phi   c     psi  gamma  E        nu    K0
30  5  0  20  100000  0.3  0.5
! Nodal coordinates (m)
10  5
-20  0
44  0
44  10
32  10
12  20
0  20
-20  10
! Element connectivity (T3), 1-based node ids
1  2  3
1  3  4
1  4  5
1  5  6
1  6  7
1  7  8
1  8  2
! Boundary conditions: 0=fixed DOF, 1=free (see app smoke .dat convention)
4
2  0  0
3  0  0
4  0  1
8  0  1
! Output nodes
8
1  2  3  4  5  6  7  8
! Solver control: tol limit incs layers  (layers=0 => traction-driven elastoplastic path)
0.02  1000  10  0
! Traction groups: mode 0 => sxx=p0, syy=p1, sxy=p2 (kPa, tension +)
! One group on six exterior edges (omit bottom 2-3 where displacements are fixed).
1
0  -90  -180  0
6
3  4
4  5
5  6
6  7
7  8
8  2
